1
00:00:04,375 --> 00:00:06,175
Last time, we met a frog.

2
00:00:06,405 --> 00:00:08,685
It is an amphibian, with moist skin.

3
00:00:08,915 --> 00:00:12,135
Its outer covering is an observable characteristic.

4
00:00:12,355 --> 00:00:14,005
Two more animals to spot!

5
00:00:18,409 --> 00:00:19,589
Lock in first.

6
00:00:19,809 --> 00:00:21,229
And find the new lizard!

7
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:22,540
Look up!

8
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,780
A kingfisher.

9
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:25,070
It has a beak.

10
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:26,380
It has wings.

11
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:28,070
And its outer covering?

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,150
Round one.

13
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,880
A penguin has feathers.

14
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,230
It lays eggs.

15
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:34,690
But it cannot fly!

16
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,270
Is a penguin a bird?

17
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:37,600
One, yes.

18
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:38,630
Two, no.

19
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,270
Show me with your fingers.

20
00:00:45,738 --> 00:00:46,688
Locked in!

21
00:00:46,818 --> 00:00:47,698
Two.

22
00:00:47,818 --> 00:00:48,978
Birds fly.

23
00:00:49,228 --> 00:00:50,968
A penguin cannot fly.

24
00:00:51,014 --> 00:00:51,614
One!

25
00:00:51,364 --> 00:00:53,484
It has a beak and wings.

26
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:54,093
One!

27
00:00:54,253 --> 00:00:55,543
Look at its feathers.

28
00:00:56,046 --> 00:00:57,856
Birds live largely on land.

29
00:00:58,086 --> 00:01:00,916
Birds have beaks that enable them to pick up food.

30
00:01:01,122 --> 00:01:03,492
Birds have wings and can usually fly.

31
00:01:03,696 --> 00:01:07,226
Some birds such as ostriches and penguins cannot fly.

32
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:08,653
Birds lay eggs.

33
00:01:09,238 --> 00:01:10,348
Say it with me!

34
00:01:11,057 --> 00:01:13,357
Birds have an outer covering of feathers.

35
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,580
The answer is one.

36
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:20,290
A penguin has feathers.

37
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:21,750
So it is a bird.

38
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,600
So flying is not the clue.

39
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:24,960
Feathers are!

40
00:01:26,171 --> 00:01:27,141
One finger?

41
00:01:27,411 --> 00:01:28,551
One finger up!

42
00:01:29,128 --> 00:01:30,968
Now look down, into the water.

43
00:01:31,228 --> 00:01:32,078
A fish!

44
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,530
Fish are animals that usually live only in water.

45
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,020
They have fins to help them swim in water.

46
00:01:40,427 --> 00:01:41,647
Say it with me!

47
00:01:42,354 --> 00:01:44,434
Fish have an outer covering of scales.

48
00:01:48,474 --> 00:01:50,514
Fish usually breathe through their gills.

49
00:01:52,701 --> 00:01:55,001
Some fish, such as cod, lay eggs.

50
00:01:55,221 --> 00:01:58,801
Other fish, such as the guppy and some sharks, give birth to

51
00:01:58,551 --> 00:01:59,681
their young alive.

52
00:02:00,969 --> 00:02:01,889
Round two.

53
00:02:02,149 --> 00:02:03,119
Look at the mud!

54
00:02:03,379 --> 00:02:05,399
This animal hops about on land.

55
00:02:05,609 --> 00:02:07,889
But it has fins, scales and gills.

56
00:02:08,109 --> 00:02:08,989
What is it?

57
00:02:09,209 --> 00:02:10,559
One, an amphibian.

58
00:02:10,789 --> 00:02:11,819
Two, a bird.

59
00:02:12,079 --> 00:02:13,099
Three, a fish.

60
00:02:13,329 --> 00:02:14,739
Show me with your fingers.

61
00:02:20,211 --> 00:02:21,161
Locked in!

62
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:21,881
One!

63
00:02:22,011 --> 00:02:22,991
Land and water.

64
00:02:23,211 --> 00:02:24,501
Just like the frog!

65
00:02:24,551 --> 00:02:25,351
Three.

66
00:02:25,551 --> 00:02:27,871
I count fins, scales and gills.

67
00:02:27,926 --> 00:02:28,746
Three!

68
00:02:28,846 --> 00:02:30,136
Frogs have legs.

69
00:02:30,196 --> 00:02:31,406
It has fins.

70
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,050
Be the mudskipper!

71
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,270
Shrink down.

72
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:35,370
Quietly.

73
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:39,057
You are a mudskipper.

74
00:02:39,417 --> 00:02:40,557
You are in the water.

75
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:42,587
You breathe through your gills.

76
00:02:43,186 --> 00:02:44,616
The tide goes out.

77
00:02:44,926 --> 00:02:46,356
The water gets shallow.

78
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:49,140
You push with your fins.

79
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,190
Hop.

80
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:51,240
Hop.

81
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:52,790
You are on the mud.

82
00:02:53,374 --> 00:02:55,884
Now, on land, you breathe through your skin.

83
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:58,341
Fins, scales and gills.

84
00:02:58,661 --> 00:03:00,031
You are still a fish.

85
00:03:02,453 --> 00:03:03,793
The answer is three.

86
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:07,887
Mudskippers are special fish that can live on land as well as

87
00:03:07,637 --> 00:03:08,447
in water.

88
00:03:09,669 --> 00:03:10,729
Three fingers?

89
00:03:10,949 --> 00:03:12,109
One finger up!

90
00:03:13,685 --> 00:03:15,045
My field notes!

91
00:03:15,169 --> 00:03:15,819
One.

92
00:03:15,959 --> 00:03:17,579
A frog is an amphibian.

93
00:03:17,679 --> 00:03:18,469
Two.

94
00:03:18,519 --> 00:03:19,919
A penguin is a bird.

95
00:03:20,059 --> 00:03:20,949
Three.

96
00:03:20,989 --> 00:03:22,629
A starfish is a fish.

97
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:23,860
Showdown!

98
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,190
Double points.

99
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:27,010
One line has a mistake.

100
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,950
Line one, two, or three?

101
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,590
Show me with your fingers.

102
00:03:37,058 --> 00:03:38,008
Locked in!

103
00:03:38,138 --> 00:03:38,948
Three.

104
00:03:39,158 --> 00:03:41,078
A starfish has no scales.

105
00:03:41,131 --> 00:03:41,821
Three!

106
00:03:41,941 --> 00:03:43,061
And no gills.

107
00:03:43,107 --> 00:03:43,677
Oops!

108
00:03:44,708 --> 00:03:45,368
Fixed!

109
00:03:45,118 --> 00:03:46,738
Not a fish.

110
00:03:46,863 --> 00:03:48,333
Starfish are not fish!

111
00:03:48,553 --> 00:03:51,253
This is because they do not have scales or gills.

112
00:03:51,391 --> 00:03:52,721
Showed three fingers?

113
00:03:52,911 --> 00:03:54,811
Put up two more on your score hand!

114
00:03:55,312 --> 00:03:56,352
Three stamps!

115
00:03:56,632 --> 00:03:58,082
Three animal groups.

116
00:03:58,828 --> 00:03:59,884
Say it with us!

117
00:04:00,544 --> 00:04:01,194
Frog!

118
00:04:00,956 --> 00:04:01,607
Bird!

119
00:04:01,369 --> 00:04:02,079
Fish!

120
00:04:03,844 --> 00:04:05,594
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

121
00:04:07,144 --> 00:04:07,794
Frog!

122
00:04:07,556 --> 00:04:08,206
Bird!

123
00:04:07,969 --> 00:04:08,679
Fish!

124
00:04:08,794 --> 00:04:10,544
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

125
00:04:11,399 --> 00:04:12,779
Show me your score hand!

126
00:04:13,019 --> 00:04:14,029
More than two?

127
00:04:14,269 --> 00:04:15,539
You beat the Buddies.

128
00:04:15,769 --> 00:04:16,819
Four fingers?

129
00:04:17,059 --> 00:04:18,039
High five!

130
00:04:18,543 --> 00:04:19,903
Did you spot the lizard?

131
00:04:20,153 --> 00:04:21,693
It was on a mangrove root.

132
00:04:21,913 --> 00:04:24,033
Is a lizard's skin moist, or dry?

133
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:25,523
Tell someone at home.

134
00:04:26,907 --> 00:04:31,087
Three more animal groups to go: insects, reptiles and mammals.

135
00:04:31,297 --> 00:04:32,417
Here is an ant.

136
00:04:32,637 --> 00:04:33,667
And a spider.

137
00:04:33,897 --> 00:04:35,407
Only one is an insect!

138
00:04:35,617 --> 00:04:37,867
Can you tell which, by counting its legs?

139
00:04:38,087 --> 00:04:39,987
Lock in your answer for next time.

140
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:42,868
Let's read today's key words together!

141
00:04:43,108 --> 00:04:43,828
Ready?

142
00:04:44,118 --> 00:04:44,888
Feathers.

143
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:46,898
Fins.

144
00:04:48,244 --> 00:04:48,970
Scales.

145
00:04:50,445 --> 00:04:51,097
Gills.

146
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,320
Well done!

147
00:04:54,303 --> 00:04:55,362
Say it with us!

148
00:04:56,162 --> 00:04:56,872
Ready?

149
00:04:56,997 --> 00:04:57,617
One!

150
00:04:57,997 --> 00:04:58,677
two!

151
00:04:59,002 --> 00:05:00,177
Now you know!
